WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.370
-Well, today was Thanksgiving,
so if you haven't gotten around

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.506
to arguing with your family
about politics yet,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.174
allow me to change that
by spending the next

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:11.610
12 to 14 minutes discussing
the 2024 presidential election

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.145
and specifically
the various ways

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:15.748
in which Donald Trump
is very bad.

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:18.017
Brace yourselves.
It's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:21.787
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:24.690
It's Thanksgiving, which means
it's the end of a long day

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.459
where everyone's
been chugging red wine

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.962
and awkwardly smiling
at uncomfortable family stories

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:32.264
like Ron DeSantis
on a debate stage.

00:00:32.264 --> 00:00:33.833
And if you're watching this
on Thanksgiving,

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.603
there's a good chance you either
are or are with a weird uncle.

00:00:37.603 --> 00:00:39.672
Now, if you're
with a weird uncle,

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.574
blink once to let us know
you're okay.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.042
And if you are a weird uncle,

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:46.012
blink 1,000 times like you did
when your niece told everyone

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:49.081
how she met her girlfriend
at Brown.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.317
Perfect. We're off. It's great
to be with all of you.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.386
And, by the way, I just want
to say I personally have

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.655
nothing against weird uncles.
We all have them.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.790
They play an integral role
in the family dynamic.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.759
That's how younger generations
learn about stuff like

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.694
pull my finger,
members-only jackets,

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.663
"Svengoolie," off-track betting,

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:07.367
and the non-pillow products
sold by Mike Lindell.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.002
"Yeah, he makes
great slippers, too,

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.103
but the liberal media
won't tell you about that.

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:13.006
He even got a whole line
of fake mustaches

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:15.375
called MyStache.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:17.510
Touch it. Feels real, right?

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.279
Yeah, they make it
from horsehair.

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:23.883
I don't know. I think they grab
the tails while they run by."

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.686
So weird uncles are fine,
but there is a delicate balance

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.321
when one enters an ecosystem.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.323
A solitary weird uncle?
That's manageable.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.325
But too many weird uncles,
and chaos is upon you.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:34.260
And that's what's happened
to American politics,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.463
which in recent years has become
dominated by weird uncles,

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:40.800
guys like Lindell or
Steve Bannon or Rudy Giuliani.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.202
In fact, the weird uncles
all seem to gravitate toward

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:45.471
each other and team up together
kind of like Voltron

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:49.341
if Voltron had a Ziploc full of
pills in his glove compartment.

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:50.909
Just this week,
Lindell was on Bannon's

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:52.344
streaming show or podcast

00:01:52.344 --> 00:01:54.847
or transmission from his volcano
lair or whatever the hell it is,

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:57.983
where Lindell claimed that a
recent judge's ruling in Georgia

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.251
that had nothing to do with him

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:00.686
and did not even
mention his name

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:03.589
had somehow vindicated him
for spreading election lies,

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:06.326
proving that he is not
a conspiracy theorist.

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.427
He even brought props
and a costume

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:10.029
to really drive home the point.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:13.132
-Well, first of all, Steve, I
get to take off my tinfoil hat.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.600
You know, that's what
that judge said.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.237
We're not a conspiracy-theory
guy anymore. Praise the Lord.

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:21.507
-First of all, I love --
I love that we're at the point

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.676
where Mike Lindell
is actually wearing the things

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:28.381
I used to ask my graphics team
to Photoshop on top of him.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.949
Second of all,
that's not what tinfoil hats

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.484
are supposed to look like.
They're pointy.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:34.854
You don't just wrap tinfoil
around a baseball cap.

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.957
You look like a cabby
from a bad sci-fi movie.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.925
Hand it to Mike Lindell,
who can do a thing

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:42.228
only crazy people do
in a way that is even crazier.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.163
If you were wearing
a regular tinfoil hat

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:46.966
on the subway, and Mike Lindell
sat down next to you in his,

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.869
you'd move to the next car.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.639
"That guy is [bleep] crazy!

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.872
Where was I?

00:02:53.872 --> 00:02:56.309
Oh, the government's
sending brainwaves."

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.177
Third, did you mean
to take off your glasses?

00:02:58.177 --> 00:02:59.746
I mean, was that part
of the costume?

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.114
You're not Clark Kent, dude.
We know it's you.

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:05.083
Look like a side character from
the "Where's Waldo" universe

00:03:05.083 --> 00:03:07.620
called Loony Lindell.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.854
I think Lindell's real fear

00:03:08.854 --> 00:03:10.422
is that if he keeps
wearing the glasses,

00:03:10.422 --> 00:03:12.024
he might see where
he screwed up the math

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:14.193
and realize he's wrong
about the election results.

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:16.829
[as Lindell]
"The vote totals were
manipulated by the machines!

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.897
You can see here
that they don't add up!

00:03:18.897 --> 00:03:21.934
And, oh, wait a second.
Oh, brother. Hold on.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:24.571
I thought that 7 was a 2.
That changes everything.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:27.172
Okay. Joe Biden's
definitely president.

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:28.908
My bad!"

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:32.411
Nonetheless, this gang
of weirdos in Trump's orbit

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:34.380
is once again
inching closer to power

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.282
as polls show
the presidential race

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.584
is essentially a dead heat
just a year before the election.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.553
Trump has promised
that this time around,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.755
he'll stock his administration
with loyalists

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.990
who obediently follow
his every command,

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.692
and his former aides
from his first term,

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:48.294
like his ex-chief of staff,
John Kelly,

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.896
have been out there
sounding the alarm

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.397
about just how bad
that would be.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.965
-"The Washington Post"
interviewed

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:54.834
16 former Trump advisers

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:58.504
who are now speaking out
against him publicly.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.975
And that includes John Kelly,
who was the longest-serving

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:04.543
chief of staff
for the former president.

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:06.712
Kelly tells the newspaper this.

00:04:06.712 --> 00:04:08.047
"What's going on in the country

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:10.883
that a single person
thinks this guy

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.919
would still be
a good president

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.754
when he's said
the things he said

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.622
and done the things he's done?

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:21.360
It's beyond my comprehension
he has the support he has.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.830
I think we're in a dangerous
zone in our country."

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.866
-I do appreciate the warning
he's trying to give us,

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.734
but Kelly saying
we're in a dangerous zone now

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.136
is like one of those
weather guys

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.972
who reports live from inside
a category-five hurricane,

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.240
clinging to a light pole

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.475
while a shark swims by
in waist-deep floodwater,

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:38.544
saying, "The wind's really
starting to pick up out here!

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:40.947
You might want
to rethink your picnic!

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.282
And if you do have any food,

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:45.484
make sure to wrap it up
like this!"

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:46.919
I also love
when it finally dawns

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.987
on these former Trump guys
how the rest of us have felt

00:04:48.987 --> 00:04:50.189
for the last seven years.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.691
It's 2023,
and suddenly they're like,

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:54.293
"Oh, goodness. I don't get it.
How can people support this guy?

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:56.496
You worked for him!
It's like if someone said,

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:58.030
"How can anyone listen
to Hall and Oates?"

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.498
And you turned around
to see who it was,

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:02.468
and it was [bleep] Oates.

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.370
So Trump's former aides
are now speaking out

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.105
because they can't believe
he's actually

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.306
in a dead heat with Biden.

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:09.174
And Trump has made his plans
extremely clear.

00:05:09.174 --> 00:05:10.376
If he wins a second term,

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.278
he'll weaponize
the Justice Department

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:14.413
to crush enemies
he's referred to as "vermin."

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:16.848
That's not an exaggeration.
That's an exact quote.

00:05:16.848 --> 00:05:18.717
"The Washington Post" reported
that Trump and his allies

00:05:18.717 --> 00:05:20.386
will seek revenge
in a second term,

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:22.154
and Trump himself
has admitted as much

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:23.623
in rallies and interviews.

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:25.891 line:0%
-According to recent
"Washington Post" reporting,

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:28.027 line:0%
"Donald Trump and his allies
have begun

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.829 line:0%
mapping out specific plans

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:33.332 line:0%
for using the federal government
to punish critics and opponents

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.601 line:0%
should he win a second term,

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.903 line:0%
with the former president
naming individuals

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:40.005 line:0%
he wants to investigate
or prosecute."

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:42.174
-We will start by exposing

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:45.712
every last crime committed
by Crooked Joe Biden

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:50.049
because now that he indicted me,
we're allowed to look at him.

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:51.784
This is third-world-country
stuff.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:54.386
Arrest your --
Arrest your opponent.

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:56.188
And that means
that I could do that, too.

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:58.657
If they want to
follow through on this,

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:01.493
yeah, it could certainly
happen in reverse.

00:06:01.493 --> 00:06:03.162
It could certainly happen
in reverse.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.430
What they've done is

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.166
they've released the genie
out of the box.

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:09.201
-Yes.

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:12.404
Famously, that is the saying.

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:14.340
They released the genie
out of the box,

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.741
they opened Pandora's Lamp,

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:19.045
and they let the cat out
of solitary confinement.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:21.313
And, look, this couldn't be
further down my list

00:06:21.313 --> 00:06:22.882
of complaints
about Donald Trump,

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:25.551
but genies live
in lamps or bottles,

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.853
you know, things with openings
that are conducive

00:06:27.853 --> 00:06:30.489
to smoke-based beings
making a dramatic exit.

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:32.658
How would a genie
even come out of a box?

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:36.095
You just rub the sides
of random DHL packages,

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:38.064
and if you get lucky,
a voice from inside says,

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.798
"I am the genie of the box!

00:06:39.798 --> 00:06:42.968
You're gonna need to poke
a hole in the side for me!"

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:45.204
And I'll tell you this much.
There's no way a box genie

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:47.206
has three wishes to give.
If a genie's in a box,

00:06:47.206 --> 00:06:49.775
that genie's in a bad place
in his life.

00:06:49.775 --> 00:06:52.578
If anything, he's gonna need
to borrow a wish from you.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.479
"Genie of the box,
I wish for fame and fortune."

00:06:54.479 --> 00:06:57.850
"Oh, that's a good one.
Wish I thought of that one.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:01.954
I used my last wish to get
Aaron Rodgers on the Jets."

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.255
[Bleep] the bed on that one.

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:06.959
Should have wished
for stronger ankles.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:11.664
Okay, I think I'm gonna
get back in my box now."

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:12.998
Also, can we go back to this?

00:07:12.998 --> 00:07:14.734
-This is third-world-country
stuff.

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:17.336
Arrest your --
Arrest your opponent.

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:19.038
And that means
that I could do that, too.

00:07:19.038 --> 00:07:21.640
-Only Trump would call something
"third-world" in one sentence

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.109
and then immediately brag about
doing it in the next sentence.

00:07:24.109 --> 00:07:25.877
"It's disgusting
what they're doing to me.

00:07:25.877 --> 00:07:28.347
Only a truly appalling,
cretinous, subhuman monster

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:30.716
would ever stoop to such
grotesque and horrifying lows.

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:34.153
Which is why I'm very excited
to announce...

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:36.555
that I will soon be doing
the exact same thing!"

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:38.424
Of course,
there's a massive difference

00:07:38.424 --> 00:07:40.225
between what Trump
is promising to do

00:07:40.225 --> 00:07:41.994
and what prosecutors
are currently doing to Trump.

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.695
Trump is facing four
different criminal cases,

00:07:43.695 --> 00:07:45.397
including one
in Washington, D.C.,

00:07:45.397 --> 00:07:46.999
for what we all saw
with our own eyes --

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:48.501
his attempt
to overturn the election.

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.403
Trump, on the other hand,
wants revenge

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:53.272
because he's still fixated
on all the investigations

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:55.141
of his very obvious
criminal behavior.

00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:57.342
At rallies, he's started
doing a new bit where

00:07:57.342 --> 00:07:59.612
he compares his indictments
to those of Al Capone,

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:01.680
although the stories
about Capone keep changing.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.048
Here's the latest version.

00:08:03.048 --> 00:08:06.786
-I've been indicted more times
than Alphonse Capone.

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:09.354
He's the most vicious
of all gangsters.

00:08:09.354 --> 00:08:11.824
If he took you to dinner
and if you didn't look proper,

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:12.992
if you laughed a little bit,

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:14.526
he might think
you're laughing at him.

00:08:14.526 --> 00:08:18.197
It's dangerous to laugh.
He'd kill you immediately.

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:21.100
He was indicted one time.
I was indicted four times.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.835
-Okay, so he definitely
is thinking

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:24.203
of the famous scene
from "Goodfellas."

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:28.240
He probably thinks Joe Pesci
is Al Capone.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:30.109
"Al Capone,
the most vicious of gangsters.

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:31.810
The only two people
who could take him down

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:35.314
were Eliot Ness
and Kevin McCallister.

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:37.149
You know, I met
Kevin McCallister once.

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:41.654
He was lost in New York.
It was very sad. Very sad."

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:43.923
Also, it shouldn't bother me
this much, but I hate --

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:45.891
I hate how he says
"Alphonse Capone."

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:49.228
He's so proud he knows
what the "Al" is short for.

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:51.363
He knows one fact,
and he's walking around

00:08:51.363 --> 00:08:53.865
like he's Ken Jennings.

00:08:53.865 --> 00:08:56.335
He probably only knows it
because a box genie told him.

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:59.271
"For my first wish,
I want to be president again."

00:08:59.271 --> 00:09:03.108
"Oh, no can do.
That's way above my pay grade.

00:09:03.108 --> 00:09:05.244
I can tell you what Al Capone's
full name is, though.

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:07.146
You want that?

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:09.782
That's not a wish, but
it's a pretty good fun factoid.

00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:13.519
Alright. I'm gonna
get back in the box. Enh."

00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:15.888
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:17.722
So Trump wants to seek revenge
on his critics

00:09:17.722 --> 00:09:20.359
because he's fixated
on all the investigations
he's been through.

00:09:20.359 --> 00:09:22.628
He's even still obsessed
with the Russia investigation.

00:09:22.628 --> 00:09:26.365
At a rally just a few days ago,
he went out of his way

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:28.233
to bring up one of
the more salacious rumors

00:09:28.233 --> 00:09:31.436
that was flying around about
his personal life back in 2017.

00:09:31.436 --> 00:09:32.671
-This is the greatest
witch hunt.

00:09:32.671 --> 00:09:35.441
It started with
Russia, Russia, Russia.

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:37.876
Remember that?
"He was with four hookers."

00:09:37.876 --> 00:09:40.345
You think that was good
that night to go up

00:09:40.345 --> 00:09:42.281
and tell my wife,
"It's not true, darling.

00:09:42.281 --> 00:09:44.883
I love you very much.
It's not true."

00:09:44.883 --> 00:09:47.419
Actually, that one she didn't
believe because she said,

00:09:47.419 --> 00:09:49.888
"He's a germaphobe.
He's not into that." You know?

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:53.426
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:56.528
"He's not into golden showers,
as they say they call them.

00:09:56.528 --> 00:09:58.097
He's not."

00:09:58.097 --> 00:09:59.932
I don't like that idea.

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:01.933
[ Applause ]

00:10:01.933 --> 00:10:03.935
No, I didn't. I thought
that would be a big problem.

00:10:03.935 --> 00:10:05.137
I was gonna have a rough night.

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:07.339
But that one,
she was very good on.

00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:11.076
She said, "No, that --
You're okay on that one."

00:10:11.076 --> 00:10:12.845
-Dude, not even Democrats
are thinking

00:10:12.845 --> 00:10:14.513
about the pee tape anymore!

00:10:14.513 --> 00:10:16.916
But when you come out
six years later

00:10:16.916 --> 00:10:19.051
and deny a story
everybody forgot about,

00:10:19.051 --> 00:10:22.554
I have to think, heh,
maybe it's true.

00:10:22.554 --> 00:10:24.657
If someone came up to you
at your 20th high-school reunion

00:10:24.657 --> 00:10:26.158
and said, "By the way,
I'm not the one

00:10:26.158 --> 00:10:27.893
who put the sardines
in your locker,"

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:31.230
then you just solved that case.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.464
My favorite part is when he said

00:10:32.464 --> 00:10:33.899
Melania didn't believe
"that one."

00:10:33.899 --> 00:10:35.467
Like there are plenty
of other stories

00:10:35.467 --> 00:10:37.302
she definitely believed.

00:10:37.302 --> 00:10:39.171
"She didn't believe
the golden-shower story,

00:10:39.171 --> 00:10:41.540
but when the news broke that
I asked a porn star to spank me

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:43.876
with a 'Forbes' magazine
while we watched 'Shark Week,'

00:10:43.876 --> 00:10:46.078
she said,
'That sounds like my Donald.'"

00:10:46.078 --> 00:10:48.913
[ Laughter ]

00:10:48.913 --> 00:10:50.215
Also, let me just say

00:10:50.215 --> 00:10:51.951
I never believed
the golden-shower story, either.

00:10:51.951 --> 00:10:53.953
I mean, Trump barely looks like
he takes regular showers.

00:10:53.953 --> 00:10:55.488
I mean, look at him.
He's always red-faced

00:10:55.488 --> 00:10:57.022
and sweating
like he's been in the kitchen

00:10:57.022 --> 00:10:58.357
all day making
Thanksgiving dinner,

00:10:58.357 --> 00:11:00.559
accidentally sticking
his own head in the oven.

00:11:00.559 --> 00:11:03.228
You don't need a doctor
to tell you this isn't healthy.

00:11:03.228 --> 00:11:05.530
Even the Butterball hotline
would take one look at this pic

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:07.399
and be like, "He's overcooked!"

00:11:07.399 --> 00:11:10.035
It looks like he should
be served on a plate

00:11:10.035 --> 00:11:12.538
next to some yams
and a green-bean casserole.

00:11:12.538 --> 00:11:14.306
[ Laughter ]

00:11:14.306 --> 00:11:16.809
So it's Thanksgiving.
It's Thanksgiving.

00:11:16.809 --> 00:11:19.578
Which means we're just under
a year away from the election.

00:11:19.578 --> 00:11:21.646
Everyone's taking stock
of where we're at.

00:11:21.646 --> 00:11:23.615
Thanks to the GOP,
our national politics

00:11:23.615 --> 00:11:26.084
has basically been turned into
a nonstop Thanksgiving dinner

00:11:26.084 --> 00:11:27.787
made up entirely
of weird uncles.

00:11:27.787 --> 00:11:29.255
And if Trump wins a second term,

00:11:29.255 --> 00:11:31.256
his administration
will be full of weird uncles,

00:11:31.256 --> 00:11:32.858
except now
they'll have real power.

00:11:32.858 --> 00:11:34.627
So let that thought
sit with you tonight

00:11:34.627 --> 00:11:36.696
while you're pouring
all of that delicious gravy

00:11:36.696 --> 00:11:38.497
all over those
oven-roasted turkeys.

00:11:38.497 --> 00:11:41.200
Honestly, I'm getting hungry
just thinking about those...

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:42.768
-Golden showers!

00:11:42.768 --> 00:11:44.503
[ Laughter ]

00:11:50.676 --> 00:11:54.079
-Happy Thanksgiving!
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:54.079 --> 00:11:57.682
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:57.682 --> 00:11:59.785 line:0%
Hey, everybody. Thanks
for watching "A Closer Look."

00:11:59.785 --> 00:12:01.486 line:0%
And as a reminder,
my brother Josh and I

00:12:01.486 --> 00:12:03.288 line:0%
have started a new podcast

00:12:03.288 --> 00:12:05.925 line:0%
called "Family Trips
with the Meyers Brothers."

00:12:05.925 --> 00:12:09.061 line:0%
We hope you listen. We hope
you like it. And see you soon.

